The glob view prints a Rust file's `//` header comment with its lines joined by a space, `(no header available)` for a file without one, and skips the unsupported `raw.txt`.
== args
input/**/*
== file input/src/with-header.rs
// Rust service worker.
// Handles background jobs.

fn run() {}
== file input/src/no-header.rs
fn ping() {}
== file input/misc/raw.txt
plain text
== stdout
glob view: input/**/*
input/src/no-header.rs (1 line): (no header available)
input/src/with-header.rs (4 lines): Rust service worker. Handles background jobs.
== stderr
== exit 0
